            "review_title": "Review at Kichi Kichi",
            "review_text": "Malcolm S.\nSingapore, Singapore571 contributions\n0\nGood value good food and interesting concept\nDec 2016 • Friends\nI had the opportunity to try this restaurant at the Vincom shopping centre branch basement 3. Walked out of the restaurant pretty impressed by the food, affordability and the service.\n\nThis is a hotpot conveyor belt restaurant. Meaning that whatever plate is on conveyor belt is free to eat and take. The cost is about USD 10 per pax for the buffet set. You also get an option to choose one of the 4 type of soups available, with 1 non-spicy option, 2 not so spicy and 1 spicy soup base. You can add additional orders of better grade beef at an additional top up. \n\nOverall, I believe this is one of the best chain restaurant that Vietnam offers and will likely be heading for overseas expansion in the near future with its cool concept. Will likely come again when visiting Vietnam!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 2, 2017",
